#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:5
msgid "AMD HSMP interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:7
msgid ""
"Newer Fam19h(model 0x00-0x1f, 0x30-0x3f, 0x90-0x9f, 0xa0-0xaf), Fam1Ah(model "
"0x00-0x1f) EPYC server line of processors from AMD support system management "
"functionality via HSMP (Host System Management Port)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:11
msgid ""
"The Fam1Ah(model 0x80-0x8f, 0xe0-0xe3) client line of processors is "
"supported as well. Those models share one mailbox and speak the Ryzen Master "
"SMC message set instead of the server HSMP message set, so the message IDs "
"accepted on them are the HSMP_CLIENT_* ones listed in arch/x86/include/uapi/"
"asm/amd_hsmp.h. The character device and ioctl interface described below are "
"the same."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:18
msgid ""
"The Host System Management Port (HSMP) is an interface to provide OS-level "
"software with access to system management functions via a set of mailbox "
"registers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:22
msgid ""
"More details on the interface can be found in chapter \"7 Host System "
"Management Port (HSMP)\" of the family/model PPR Eg: https://docs.amd.com/v/"
"u/en-US/55898_B1_pub_0_50"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:27
msgid ""
"HSMP interface is supported on EPYC line of server CPUs, MI300A (APU) and "
"the Fam1Ah client models listed above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:32
msgid "HSMP device"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:34
msgid ""
"amd_hsmp driver under drivers/platforms/x86/amd/hsmp/ has separate driver "
"files for ACPI object based probing, platform device based probing and for "
"the common code for these two drivers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:38
msgid ""
"Kconfig option CONFIG_AMD_HSMP_PLAT compiles plat.c and creates amd_hsmp.ko. "
"Kconfig option CONFIG_AMD_HSMP_ACPI compiles acpi.c and creates "
"hsmp_acpi.ko. Selecting any of these two configs automatically selects "
"CONFIG_AMD_HSMP. This compiles common code hsmp.c and creates hsmp_common.ko "
"module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:43
msgid ""
"Both the ACPI and plat drivers create the miscdevice /dev/hsmp to let user "
"space programs run hsmp mailbox commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:46
msgid "The ACPI object format supported by the driver is defined below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/x86/amd_hsmp.rst:48
msgid ""
"$ ls -al /dev/hsmp crw-r--r-- 1 root root 10, 123 Jan 21 21:41 /dev/hsmp"
msgstr ""

